hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15954","Mus'ab ibn al-Miqdam and Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, they said, Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriya: that Ma'n ibn Yazid narrated to him, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my father and my grandfather, and he addressed for me and married me, and I disputed to him. My father Yazid had gone out with dinars to give in charity, and placed them with a man in the mosque, so I took them and came to him with them. So he said: By Allah, you are not whom I intended with them. So I disputed with him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You have what you intended, O Yazid, and you, O Ma'n, have what you took."
"15955","Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said, Suhayl ibn Dhira' narrated to me, that he heard Ma'n ibn Yazid, or Abu Ma'n, say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gather in your mosques, and when a people gather, let them inform me. He said: So we gathered before people and came to him, and he came walking with us until he sat with us. Then a speaker of us spoke and said: Praise belongs to Allah, for praise there is no limit short of Him, and beyond Him there is no outlet, and the like of this. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became angry and stood up. So we blamed one another, and some of us blamed others, and we said: Allah singled us out with him coming to us before people, and that he did such-and-such. He said: So we came to him and found him in the mosque of Banu so-and-so. We spoke to him, and he came walking with us until he sat in his gathering in which he had been, or near it. Then he said: Praise belongs to Allah; what Allah wills He puts before Him, and what He wills He puts behind Him, and among eloquence is magic. Then he turned to us, commanded us, spoke to us, and taught us."
"15956","Affan narrated to us, he said, Abu Awana narrated to us, he said, Asim ibn Kulayb narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Juwayriya narrated to me, he said: I found a red jar with dinars in it during the rule of Mu'awiya in the land of Rum. And over us was a man of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of Banu Sulaym called Ma'n ibn Yazid. So I brought it for him to divide among the Muslims, and he gave me like what he gave a man of them. Then he said: Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and saw him do it, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no nafl except after the khums, I would have given you. He said: Then he took and offered me from his share, but I refused him. I said: I am no more entitled to it than you."
"15957","Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik and Surayj ibn al-Nu'man narrated to us, they said, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Abu al-Juwayriya, he said, Affan narrated to us, he said, Abu Awana narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Juwayriya narrated to us, from Ma'n ibn Yazid, he said: I pledged the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I and my father and my grandfather, and I disputed to him and he judged me successful, and he addressed for me and married me."
